an interviewer ask me that let suppose, you have 3 api request calling in react,one take 5 sec,one take 10 sec,one take 30 sec,how can i optimize the speed and his behaviour


🔴 Problem

You have 3 APIs:

API 1 → 5 sec
API 2 → 10 sec
API 3 → 30 sec
❌ Wrong Approach (Sequential Calls)
await api1();
await api2();
await api3();

👉 Total time = 45 sec (BAD)

✅ Correct Approach 1: Parallel Calls
await Promise.all([api1(), api2(), api3()]);

👉 Total time = 30 sec (Best possible)

✅ Correct Approach 2: Show Data Early (Better UX)
useEffect(() => {
  api1().then(setData1); // show after 5s
  api2().then(setData2); // show after 10s
  api3().then(setData3); // show after 30s
}, []);

👉 User sees UI step by step
👉 Not waiting for slow API

⚠️ Important Concept

👉 Actual performance = how fast API runs
👉 Perceived performance = how fast user feels UI

🟡 Suspense (Simple Explanation)

👉 Suspense helps show UI when data is ready

❌ Wrong Use of Suspense
<Suspense fallback={<Loader />}>
  <Component1 />   // has 3 APIs inside
</Suspense>

👉 UI waits 30 sec (slowest API) ❌

✅ Correct Use (Split Components)
import { Suspense } from "react";

function App() {
  return (
    <>
      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading Data 1...</p>}>
        <Data1 />
      </Suspense>

      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading Data 2...</p>}>
        <Data2 />
      </Suspense>

      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading Data 3...</p>}>
        <Data3 />
      </Suspense>
    </>
  );
}
✅ Inside Each Component
function Data1() {
  const data = use(fetchApi1()); // React 19
  return <div>Data1: {data}</div>;
} // React 19
🎯 Result
Data1 shows in 5 sec
Data2 shows in 10 sec
Data3 shows in 30 sec

👉 UI loads step by step ✅

🔑 Suspense Key Idea

👉 “Split UI based on data dependency”

🔵 TanStack Query (Why Use It?)

Even if APIs are separate, it gives extra benefits:

✅ 1. Parallel Fetching (Automatic)
useQuery(['api1'], api1);
useQuery(['api2'], api2);
useQuery(['api3'], api3);

👉 All run together automatically

✅ 2. Caching

👉 Data is saved
👉 No need to call API again

✅ 3. Deduplication

👉 Same API called in multiple places
👉 Only ONE request is sent

✅ 4. Background Refetch

👉 Updates data without blocking UI

✅ 5. Built-in States

👉 No need for manual:

loading
error handling
✅ 6. Works with Suspense
useQuery({
  queryKey: ['api1'],
  queryFn: api1,
  suspense: true
});
🟢 useTransition (Important)

👉 DOES NOT make API faster ❌
👉 Only improves UI responsiveness ✅

Use for:

heavy UI updates
smooth typing experience

